Section/subsection name: Introduction
Content: We introduce HENN , a structural property for hierarchical graph-based indices in ANN search that unifies theoretical guarantees with practical efficiency. By organizing layers as \ud835\udf00-nets, HENN achieves provable polylogarithmic query time while retaining a simple and implementable design. We further provided a probabilistic analysis ofHNSW , shedding light on the reasons behind its strong empirical performance. To support practical adoption, we developed a budget-aware algorithm for \ud835\udf00-net construction, allowing practitioners to balance preprocessing time against recall quality.

