Section/subsection name: Related Work
Content: The nearest neighbor (NN) problem is central to many applications in computer science and engineering. In high-dimensional spaces, the curse of dimensionality makes it challenging for classical methods like k-d trees [5], ball trees [53], or Delaunay triangulations [26] to scale effectively. Hierarchical graph-based indices (HENN) have emerged as a promising solution that combines the best of both worlds: they offer provable polylogarithmic query time while retaining a simple and implementable design.

